**Files read:** target class; `AlreadyExistsExceptionTest`, `EngineTraitTest` (style/static-mock patterns); `ProductTypeTest` run as coverage control; `pom.xml`; the duplicate test-source `OfferGraphQLClient.java`; the memory file.

**Iterations:** test compiled on 2nd attempt (generic `send()` inference fixed via `doReturn`); green thereafter. Extra iterations were diagnostic — isolating the coverage cause (duplicate vs package/dir mismatch vs instrumentation) via controlled exec runs.

**Recommendation (needs your go-ahead, since it touches src/main):** move the file to `src/main/java/com/intermarche/valuation/client/OfferGraphQLClient.java` (matching its package) and delete the stale `src/test/.../client/OfferGraphQLClient.java` duplicate. After that, this test class should report full branch coverage with no code change.
