**Result:** new test class `StoreGroupUiResourceTest` (no prior test existed), 13 tests, all green; targeted `verify` → BUILD SUCCESS.

**Branch coverage: 60/60 by manual enumeration.**
JaCoCo reports `BRANCH_MISSED=60, BRANCH_COVERED=0` for the class — i.e. **zero attribution**, exactly as recorded in memory ([quarkus-jacoco-only-quarkustest]): this project's jacoco-report only measures `@QuarkusTest` runs, so plain JUnit+Mockito suites always read 0%. I confirmed the blindspot rather than a real gap: the sibling plain-unit classes `OfferUiResource` (102 branches) and `LookupResource` (36 branches) — both fully tested and green — likewise show `0` covered. Coverage is therefore enumerated manually:

- **`save`** — payload guard `payload==null || groups==null` (both arms + accepted); `error!=null` (rejected/accepted).
- **`apply`** — `code==null || isBlank` (null / blank / valid); `group==null` (create / reuse); `name==null || isBlank` ternary (all three arms → A null, B blank, C populated); `!byCode.containsKey` (kept / removed); `findParentsOf` loop (with parent / without); `storeCodes!=null` & `childCodes!=null` (present / absent); `store==null` & `child==null` (found / missing); `reaches(...)` cycle gate (clean / circular).
- **`reaches`** — `child.code.equals(target)` (hit via B→A / miss); `visited.add` (fresh / already-visited diamond); recursive result (true cycle / false) + loop-exhausted return.
- **`buildModelJson`** — group & store loops (populated / empty); `store.address==null` ternary (both arms).
- **`canWrite`** — `securityContext!=null && isUserInRole` (null ctx / non-admin / admin).

**Justified residue:** the `catch` in `buildModelJson` (serialization fallback) is unreachable — the model is a `LinkedHashMap` of `String`/`List<String>` values that Jackson never fails on, and any upstream failure (e.g. a null in `sorted()`) throws before the `try`. It is a defensive line-coverage miss, not a branch (JaCoCo does not count exception-handler edges as branches).

**Files read:** `StoreGroupUiResource.java` (target), `StoreGroup.java`, `Store.java`/`Adresse.java` (fields), and test conventions from `OfferUiResourceTest.java`, `LookupResourceTest.java`, `RejectedHierarchyMapperTest.java`; plus bytecode disassembly of `StoreGroupUiResource.class` and `OfferUiResource.class`, and `jacoco.csv`.

**Iterations:** 2 to green. The first run failed because I initially assumed `mockStatic(StoreGroup.class)` would intercept the inherited `list`/`listAll` — the bytecode shows the invokestatic owner is `StoreGroup`, but Mockito intercepts inherited statics by **declaring class**, so those calls hit the real `PanacheEntityBase` body and threw. Fixed by intercepting `list`/`listAll` via `mockStatic(PanacheEntityBase.class)` (custom finders `findByCode`/`findParentsOf` stay on the entity mocks), disambiguating the two identical `list("order by code")` calls in `buildModelJson` with consecutive stubbing.

**src/main:** untouched.
